1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:07,475
Professor Azad Moradi opened the last blank
page of a notebook he'd bought in 1973.

2
00:00:07,515 --> 00:00:12,006
Yesterday's song from the
square still rang in his ears.

3
00:00:12,046 --> 00:00:18,560
The smoke outside was thinner than yesterday's
— the effect of the 72-hour pause.

4
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,557
Whether that meant peace
or simply a held breath,

5
00:00:22,597 --> 00:00:28,349
fifty-three years of teaching philosophy
hadn't taught him how to know.

6
00:00:28,389 --> 00:00:30,893
He picked up his pen and wrote:

7
00:00:30,933 --> 00:00:35,323
“Fifty-three years ago, on
this notebook's first page,

8
00:00:35,363 --> 00:00:40,000
I wrote — truth is uncomfortable,
but a lie hurts longer.

9
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:45,502
Today, on the last page, I write
this: freedom is uncomfortable too.

10
00:00:45,542 --> 00:00:47,848
But repression hurts longer.”

11
00:00:47,888 --> 00:00:49,709
He closed the notebook.

12
00:00:49,749 --> 00:00:53,228
From the courtyard, the
singing rose again.
